desc(
	mode: "source"
	language: "general"
	title: "Hooks Sensitive File Access Bash"
	title_zh: "检测到Hooks Sensitive File Access Bash",
	type: vuln
	level: middle
	rule_id: "source-config-hooks-sensitive-file-access-bash"
	risk: "information-exposure"
	desc: <<<DESC
Migrated from Semgrep rule `hooks-sensitive-file-access-bash` (/tmp/semgrep-rules/ai/ai-best-practices/hooks-sensitive-file-access/hooks-sensitive-file-access-bash.yaml).
Original message: Hook input from jq flows into a file operation without checking for sensitive files. Claude Code and Cursor hooks receive JSON input that may reference sensitive files such as ~/.ssh/*, ~/.aws/credentials, or .env files. Filter or block access to sensitive paths using realpath and a validation check before performing file operations.

CWE: CWE-538: Insertion of Sensitive Information into Externally-Accessible File or Directory
References:
- https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/claude-code/hooks
- https://cursor.com/docs/agent/hooks
DESC
	solution: <<<SOLUTION
Review the flagged code and follow the framework's secure coding guidance: use safe APIs, escape output, and avoid hardcoded credentials.
SOLUTION
	alert_min: 1
	"file://pos.sh": <<<POS
$('S|	 

	 jq.fxJDz>cAL?) 	
	
		rm 	  
	
$
POS
	"safefile://neg.sample": <<<NEG
# safe sample
no secrets here
just regular code
NEG
)

${*.sh}.pattern_regex(/\$\(.*\|\s*jq\b[^)]*\)[\s\S]*?\n\s*(cat|rm|cp|mv)\s+\$/) as $p0
${*.bash}.pattern_regex(/\$\(.*\|\s*jq\b[^)]*\)[\s\S]*?\n\s*(cat|rm|cp|mv)\s+\$/) as $p1
$p0 + $p1 as $hit
alert $hit for {
	level: "middle",
	title: "Hooks Sensitive File Access Bash",
	title_zh: "检测到Hooks Sensitive File Access Bash",
	message: "Hooks Sensitive File Access Bash",
}
